            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 73-year-old female patient. She was admitted on 08/09/2015 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), presenting with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. On examination, she showed signs of significant airflow obstruction. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs and oxygen saturation were closely monitored throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with clinical improvement. She is discharged home with oral prednisolone taper and optimised inhaler therapy. I recommend close follow-up and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
